RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
--------------------
Excalidraw — @excalidraw/excalidraw 0.18.1 — MIT
  https://github.com/excalidraw/excalidraw
  The canvas text faces (Excalifont/Virgil hand-drawn styles and the UI
  fallback families) are fetched at runtime from Excalidraw's own font
  assets and are NOT redistributed by this project. If you self-host them
  (see "Font origin" in README.md), review each family's licence first:
  the hand-drawn faces are published by Excalidraw under CC BY 4.0, most
  UI families are SIL OFL 1.1. This project removes esm.sh from its CSP
  only when those fonts are served locally.

98.css 0.1.21 — MIT — Copyright (c) 2020 Jordan Scales
  https://github.com/jdan/98.css
  Ships the "Pixelated MS Sans Serif" web font that serves as Paint97's
  UI face (replacing a proprietary TTF that was NOT redistributable).

@react95/core 9.8.4 — MIT — React95
  https://github.com/React95/React95
  Its GlobalStyle embeds three base64 @font-face data URIs of Microsoft
  Sans Serif (© Microsoft; conversion by LR Software) that carry no
  redistribution grant. The build strips those rules (stripEmbeddedFonts
  in vite.config.ts) so they never reach dist/, and re-declares the
  "MS Sans Serif" family name over 98.css's MIT pixel faces instead;
  scripts/check-assets.mjs fails if an embedded font ever reappears.
  react95's MIT code (style resets, scrollbar styling, components) is
  used normally.

react / react-dom 19.3.0 — MIT — Meta Platforms, Inc.

clippyjs 0.1.0 (CDN fallback only, version-pinned by CSP) — MIT — Pi0
  https://github.com/pi0/clippyjs

@wllama/wllama 3.8.1 — MIT — Xuan Son NGUYEN
  https://github.com/ngxson/wllama
  WebAssembly build of llama.cpp for browsers — the Ask Clippy runtime
  (lazy-loaded, single-threaded, optional WebGPU). Its 8.7 MB wllama.wasm
  is served from our own origin; its worker code ships inside our bundle.

